{"_id":"6925a5467c7d1fa20e769215","roadmapSlug":"elasticsearch","nodeId":"4-hkqr1z0p56K0HzbifEs","description":"# Query DSL\n\nQuery DSL (Domain Specific Language) is a JSON-based language used to define and execute search queries in Elasticsearch. It provides a structured way to express complex search criteria, including boolean logic, term matching, range queries, and more, allowing users to precisely specify what data they want to retrieve.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Query DSL","url":"https://www.elastic.co/docs/explore-analyze/query-filter/languages/querydsl","_id":"69284397467651eddb61ae52"},{"type":"official","title":"Get started with Query DSL search and filters","url":"https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/query-languages/query-dsl/full-text-filter-tutorial","_id":"69284397467651eddb61ae53"},{"type":"article","title":"Elasticsearch Queries: A Guide to Query DSL","url":"https://logz.io/blog/elasticsearch-queries/","_id":"69284397467651eddb61ae54"},{"type":"article","title":"Elasticsearch Query DSL Examples","url":"https://opster.com/guides/elasticsearch/search-apis/elasticsearch-query-dsl-examples/","_id":"69284397467651eddb61ae55"},{"type":"video","title":"Elasticsearch query DSL","url":"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLGZAAioH7ZlMQGCt8GeAaJLvgehhq-gEK","_id":"69284397467651eddb61ae56"}],"createdAt":"2025-11-25T12:47:02.344Z","updatedAt":"2025-11-27T12:27:03.094Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/elasticsearch/content/4-hkqr1z0p56K0HzbifEs.md"}